  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nBig bubble and absolutely no trouble. A prolonged period of dry\nconditions is expected with high pressure remaining over the\nregion for at least the next week. Days will see high\ntemperatures in the 60s. Expect large diurnal temperature\nswings, with mostly clear conditions at night and light winds\nmaking way for efficient radiational cooling. Lows will\ngenerally be in the 30s, but a few nights could see lows dip\ninto the 20s. \n\nFire weather will be the one thing we will need to keep an eye\non over the next week. Relative humidity could dip to or below\n30% during the peak heating hours of the afternoon, but at this\ntime, winds appear that they will fairly light through the\nperiod. Dry, dead leaf litter is always a concern for wildfire\nstarts this time of year, so a prolonged dry period could make\nthis Fall season more favorable for wildfire activity.",
